{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" of Mixpanel’s track API, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can send","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events to a Mixpanel project’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and Mixpanel’s limits:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let mixpanel = try HTTPDestination.mixpanel(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    region: .eu,  \/\/ or .us or .india, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is a JSON array of content type ","type":"text"},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one object per record, oldest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first, each with two members: ","type":"text"},{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as it is, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s stored properties by name, then these members:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; left out for a record with no session","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$insert_id"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds it; the record’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when its context has no session","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0\""},{"type":"text","text":", so Mixpanel adds no location from the request’s address"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked, in whole milliseconds since 1970"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The project token","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$user_id"},{"type":"text","text":", and no other device"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier. Mixpanel counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so its unique users are sessions. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":") is its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anonymous user, linked to nothing, rather than an event with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":", which Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"would attribute to no user, or to a hash of the request’s address. Mixpanel treats two events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":" as one. A record a store recovers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after a relaunch keeps its session, so it goes out with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_id"},{"type":"text","text":" of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its first send, and Mixpanel treats it as the copy it had already stored, if it had. The record’s vendor identifier and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, an element of an array is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel cuts each string down to 255 characters. It drops an event of 255 properties or more,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counting the members above and the default properties below, one holding an array of 255"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements or more, and one whose property nests objects more than 3 deep, though it answers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"200: the encoder enforces these limits, leaving such a record out of the request."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"type":"text","text":" also holds Mixpanel’s default properties, named as its Swift SDK names them, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each of the keys the record’s context has a value for:"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version_string"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_build_number"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The version and build, each left out when ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$model","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The model"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$wifi","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Whether the connection is Wi-Fi","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operating system’s name and version"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":", as Mixpanel’s own events’ do, one with a property named as one Mixpanel reads for itself,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one past Mixpanel’s limits on properties, array elements or nesting, one whose event isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":" Mixpanel takes, one tracked more than 119 hours (5 days less an hour) before the batch"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is encoded or more than an hour after, and one too large for Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, gives each a deadline 119 hours after its oldest record was tracked, and makes none"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for it. Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"answers a request it reads with 200, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" retries one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one it rejects, such as with 400, 401 or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"413. It answers 200 as well to a request in which it finds no valid event, and says so in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"body: with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbose=1"},{"type":"text","text":", which the destination’s endpoint sets, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{\"status\": 0, \"error\": ...}"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" reads that as rejected, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" drops the request and reports it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with Mixpanel’s error. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"status"},{"type":"text","text":" of 1 means only that one event or more was well formed, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that the token names a project, so a wrong region, or a token of no project, may still be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"answered 200 with nothing stored: check the project’s Live View after setting it up."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The track API ingests only events from the last 5 days, and answers 200 while storing nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for an older one. So a record older than that, such as one a store kept through a long time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"offline, is dropped and reported rather than sent: left out when its batch is encoded","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError\/timestampOutsideWindow","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), or, when its request is still being retried","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at the deadline, dropped with the request and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The hour to spare is for a queue on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Mixpanel’s side and clocks that disagree. Mixpanel also rejects an event more than an hour in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the future, so a record tracked more than an hour after its batch is encoded is left out as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError\/timestampOutsideWindow","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" too.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record sent again keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":". The bytes are the same for the same records on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","externalID":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","modules":[{"name":"MixpanelEncoding"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder.swift#L98","fileName":"MixpanelBatchEncoder.swift"}},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/init(projectToken:plan:limit:now:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncodin